        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "924b5885-1c7e-5089-9337-13b43325a3fb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-François Clervoy, Thomas Reiter, Daisuke Enomoto\n- Organizations: CNES, ESA, NASA, German Air Force\n- Missions: Space Shuttle missions, STS-121, Expedition 14, Soyuz TMA-9\n- Places: Frankfurt, West Germany, ISS, Star City, Moscow, Russia\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-François André Clervoy was born on 19 November 1958 and is a French engineer and a CNES and ESA astronaut.\n- Thomas Arthur Reiter was born on 23 May 1958 in Frankfurt, West Germany.\n- Jean-François Clervoy is a veteran of three NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Thomas Reiter is a retired European astronaut and a Brigadier General in the German Air Force.\n- On 6 July 2006, Thomas Reiter arrived at the ISS aboard Space Shuttle Discovery during mission STS-121 and joined Expedition 14.\n- Daisuke Enomoto trained at Star City, Moscow in Russia to fly with two members of Expedition 14 aboard Soyuz TMA-9, which was launched on 18 September 2006.\n- Thomas Reiter was working as ESA Interagency Coordinator and Advisor to the Director General at the European Space Agency.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5ab04e1e-2108-53af-b518-752c11b6bb70",
        "text": "Page: Jean-François Clervoy. Sentence: Jean-François André Clervoy (born 19 November 1958) is a French engineer and a CNES and ESA astronaut.\nPage: Jean-François Clervoy. Sentence: He is a veteran of three NASA Space Shuttle missions.\nPage: Thomas Reiter. Sentence: Thomas Arthur Reiter (born 23 May 1958 in Frankfurt, West Germany) is a retired European astronaut and is a Brigadier General in the German Air Force currently working as ESA Interagency Coordinator and Advisor to the Director General at the European Space Agency (ESA).\nPage: Expedition 14. Sentence: They joined Thomas Reiter, who had arrived at the ISS on 6 July 2006 aboard Space Shuttle \"Discovery\" during mission STS-121.\nPage: Daisuke Enomoto. Sentence: He had trained at Star City, Moscow in Russia to fly with two members of Expedition 14 on board Soyuz TMA-9, which was launched on September 18, 2006.",
